---
source: minijinja-go
description: "Keyword arguments are a map[string]Value in Go, so splatting a map with integer keys into them turns the keys into strings (Rust keeps them as integers)."
---
[1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9]
[1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9]
[1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9]
[1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9]
[1, 2, {'one': 1, 'two': 2}]
[1, 2, {'one': 1, 'two': 2}]
[1, 2, {'one': 1, 'two': 2}]
[1, 2, 3, 4, {'8': 8, '9': 9}]
[1, 2, 3, 4, {'8': 8, '9': 9}]
